# What `tools/record-session.sh` leaves behind. The *recording* a layout was
# pinned to is evidence and is committed by hand —
# `assetto-corsa-competizione-20260816-2051.txt` is what the ACC layout tests
# are asserted against. The bridge's own log beside it is not evidence of
# anything, and a run that recorded no movement is worse than nothing: a page
# of constants looks like a measurement.
*-bridge.log

# The site, past the front door.
#
# `site/index.html` stays tracked: it is the landing, and GitHub Pages publishes
# it as a mirror of the front door — its links point at the domain, so that copy
# opens onto the real thing. Everything below is served only from
# proengineer.app and is kept off GitHub deliberately: the generator, the
# fragments it builds from, the shared stylesheet, and the pages themselves.
#
# These files therefore exist in exactly two places — this working copy and the
# web server. Git is not backing them up. Keep a copy somewhere outside the
# repository, the same way site/deploy.sh has always had to be kept.
site/deploy.sh
site/build.py
site/inline-css.py
site/pages/
site/assets/
site/ac/
site/acc/
site/games/
site/features/
site/compare/
site/technical/
site/download/
site/faq/
